LANTERN / TWO REUSED INK CONTAINERS / OPEN AND HOLD

Assets: masons_tool_chest and provision_hopper. These extend existing static art,
not the already animated pilgrim chest, iron lockbox, or shrine reliquary.

ART AND MOTION
Seven distinct transparent 1024 x 1024 raster poses each. Clean ink/cel artwork
reused from Lantern_Containers01_CleanInk. This is component-animated illustrated
art: source-painted surfaces rendered through the original exact orthographic
hinge rig, with authored discrete pose timing. It is not seven independently
redrawn cels, a freshly generated design, or a 3D character animation.
No image generation or generative editing occurred for this extension.
No upscaling. Original texture sampling is bicubic. Proofs are downsampled.

PLAYBACK
Use runtime/<asset>/clip.json. 60 Hz tick holds, no interpolation, no blending.
Idle holds frame 00 until an authorized interaction. Play open once, then hold
frame 06 indefinitely. The tiny hinge overshoot in frame 05 settles to the original
open geometry in frame 06. Do not automatically reverse or restart.
Loot is not painted in any frame. Invoke loot_spawn once on entry to frame 04,
using the specified tick. Gate interactions to prevent repeated rewards.
Unlocking/access checks and all loot spawning are game logic.

REGISTRATION
1024 px untrimmed canvas. Fixed ground pivot top-left origin: [512, 802].
Unity-style bottom-left normalized pivot: [0.5, 0.216796875]. Camera elevation
35.2643897 degrees; azimuth 45 degrees; exact original orthographic matrix.
All base geometry is fixed, and the lower-body pixel region is regression-tested.
Atlas 4 columns x 2 rows, 1024 px cells, row-major. Last cell empty.
No atlas padding: add engine extrusion if using bilinear atlas sampling, or import
individual PNGs. Disable automatic trimming and preserve canvas/pivot on import.

REBUILD
Python 3.10+, Pillow and NumPy. Run: python rebuild.py
Optional MP4 proof: install ffmpeg and run: python rebuild.py --video
Source files, original masters and original prompts are included. Rebuild needs
no network, model call, machine-specific absolute path, or Unity installation.
Source build_containers.py is the preserved original helper; use rebuild.py as
entry point because this focused pack deliberately includes only two designs.

QA AND LIMITATIONS
proof/qa.json records distinct poses, fixed lower body, clipping and endpoint handling.
The closed endpoint is the original static render. The open endpoint preserves
the original design and geometry; its lower-body alpha is normalized to the closed
body to fix an inherited double-composite edge-opacity discontinuity.
The body wall/rim mapping is coherent; painted recess detail remains artistic.
Baked shading does not relight. Validate engine colliders, sorting, PPU and chosen
on-screen scale. No engine import or gameplay test was performed. The MP4 uses
an opaque dark review background; runtime PNGs retain native transparency.
The original art has fixed handles and keyplates; no unlocking character/hand is
shown. These clips open the lid after game logic grants access.
